'''Baby Gao''' is an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] that was added in [[Version 5.0 Update|Version 5.0]]. He can be unlocked by rolling the [[Cat Capsule|Rare Cat Capsule]] during the [[UBERFEST (Gacha Event)|UBERFEST]] and [[SUPERFEST (Gacha Event)|SUPERFEST]] events. Just like most UBERFEST exclusives, Baby Gao has varying stats between forms, providing different usage in various situations.

{{Cat Info
|ID = 269
|rarity = UR
|name1 = Baby Gao
|name2 = Mighty Lord Gao
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Mighty Lord Gao''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal Form'''===
Baby Gao, when stacked, will demolish traited enemies that don't outrange him thanks to his [[Strong Against|Strong]] ability. Baby Gao is comparable to [[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasa Jizo]], [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]], and [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]]. He has almost the same stats as Jizo, but has a lower speed and attack rate. He can also be used as a better [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]] in almost every way, though again his subpar range (310 < 350) does hamper him despite having increased durability, DPS and knockbacks.

As with the aforementioned disposable attackers, Baby Gao can be used alongside them to provide extra DPS against enemies that do not outrange them.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Mighty Lord Gao is simple, but powerful nonetheless. Use him exactly like how you use [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Wolf]]. The differences just lay in stats. Mighty Lord Gao has an average attack rate and knockback count, but also has an unusually high 470 range and [[Immune to Waves|Wave Immunity]], and this wins him some matchups, with Wave Immunity making him a strong anti-Wave choice. More importantly, Mighty Lord Gao set the near decade-old tradition of UBERFEST units targeting all traits barring Traitless. Here, he is [[Strong Against]] all Traited enemies. This gives him an incredible effective DPS of 9.3K at Lv.30 (7.8K without fruit Treasures), setting the gold standard for Uber backliners. Strong Against also boosts Mighty Lord Gao's bulk, raising it to an effective 161K at Lv.30 (129K without fruit Treasures), which lets him take piercing attacks remarkably well. With stats like these, Mighty Lord Gao becomes a strong generalist backliner, one who you can throw in almost any Traited stages and expect good results from. Furthermore, especially with how good his bulk is, you may want to use him even when you have specialist backliners, particularly in mixed stages.

Mighty Lord Gao has some flaws in his otherwise well-rounded kit, though. For one, he doesn't target Traitless, making his stats much worse against them. Despite this, Mighty Lord Gao still retains usable DPS and a great 470 range, and has Wave Immunity for some Traitless enemies like [[Dober P.D]], so don't rule him out completely against Traitless stages. Mighty Lord Gao is also vulnerable to [[Curse|Curse]], which disables his Strong Against ability and thus much of his effective stats. Though in practice, due to his range, Mighty Lord Gao really only fears Relic Snipers like [[Loris]]. The most glaring flaw in Gao's kit is that he costs a very high 6000¢, and has a long 144s recharge time. Try to protect each Mighty Lord Gao to the best of your ability. The 5% chance to Critical Hit can be disregarded in most circumstances, but the damage is usually high enough to completely eviscerate even a [[Metal Cyclone]]. It can be worth bringing him for the sole purpose of praying for a gamechanging crit on an annoying Metal enemy.

